<title>PERU: Peru sells two fish plants for $14.5 million.</title>
<headline>Peru sells two fish plants for $14.5 million.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Peruvian government on Friday sold two fish oil and fishmeal plants for $14.5 million to local companies, privatization officials said.</p>
<p>Pesquera Rubio won the auction of state fishing company Pesca Peru's Ilo Sur plant for $7.5 million, while Hayduck bought the Ilo Norte unit for $7.04 million.</p>
<p>Pesca Peru is in the midddle of a piecemeal privatization process.</p>
<p>((--Maria-Belen Moran, Lima Newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
